ate read green).\n21\tD4 — SIX independent readings of the `/^OWED/` prefix at five instrument sites; three strip the\n22\t`READER <version>` prefix first, and `bracket-witness.js` and `light-cone.js` DO NOT — so the day a\n23\t`READER <v> OWED` row lands in swallow-ledger or bracket-ledger, swallow reads it owed and light-cone\n24\treads it ruled, and light-cone's own gate goes quiet on it. 76 live `READER … OWED` rows today, all\n25\tin darkness-ledger.\n26\tD5 — judgements live in TWO homes: 20 corpus/*.txt and 9 JSON data tiddlers; colour-witness reads\n27\tone of each.\n28\tD6 — three tools wearing a flag account for six gates (engine/behaviour, still/reach,\n29\toverreach-host/cut). D7 — snap-tid and snap-meta are one tool, one scope, two globs.\n30\tD8 — a duplication the house's own ward CANNOT SEE: one-implementation.test.js filters out\n31\t`*.test.js`, and inside that blind spot sit a byte-identical `scopesOn` helper in two invariants and\n32\t`source ./grammars.sh` inlined in two more — the exact work tokenizer.js holds.\n33\t\n34\t## Vocabulary drifts\n35\tV1 file-kind suffix: 12 ledger-shaped files, only 10 named `-ledger`; expected-divergence and\n36\tmust-fail are unsuffixed ledgers; 7 single-number ratchets split 4 floor / 3 ceiling, and\n37\t`attribute-kind-ceiling` holds a count that may FALL while `coverage-floor` holds one that may RISE —\n38\tthe filename encodes direction and gets it wrong once. colour-pair exists as both a ledger and a floor.\n39\tV2 three spellings of over-reading (OVERREACH / overbound / overreach).\n40\tV3 `MISS` is a HOMONYM across two ledgers that share one codec (line-grain dark vs character-grain\n41\tunmarked).\n42\tV4 four words for one lifecycle: stale / explains nothing / retires against `unruled` which names the\n43\topposite side; `idle` already exists in divergence-staleness and has not won.\n44\tV5 eight reason prefixes; only HOST and READER have a shared reader.\n45\tV6 444 `punctuation.definition` against 63 `punctuation.separator` and 8 `punctuation.section`, with\n46\tSCOPE-NAMES ruling nothing about which sub-family a mark takes.\n47\t\n48\t## Record duplications\n49\tR1 the migration headline exists in four places; the weld holds three hand-written restatement\n50\tregexes; TWO further restatements say 111 where the certified number is 110 (MIGRATION:36,\n51\tSCOPE-NAMES:20) — inside welded files. R2 LEDGER:1294 states 585/122/247 against the certified\n52\t556/110/245. R3 \"65 bundled themes\" stated across 8 files, welded nowhere. R4 contrast-witness's\n53\t`BAR = 16` is a literal while the ledger's prose derives it as a quarter of 65. R5 only 6 numbers in\n54\tthe whole record carry a machine twin, none in the LEDGER's 1840 lines. R6 the README's gate list is\n55\ta hand enumeration: 25 distinct names, 3 duplicated bullets, 37 of the 49 gates unnamed, and the weld\n56\tonly checks that a named script exists. R7 GateReport-Doc.tid says \"Seventeen instruments stand in\n57\ttools/\" while gate-report.js's own header says the manifest counts them. R8 two differently-keyed\n58\tenumerations of what is not a gate (a name-prefix regex and a reasons list) — and the regex form\n59\talready hid two CI instruments once.\n60\t\n61\t## L-Prime and archaeology, as counts\n62\tCopulas per line: docs/scope-naming-prior-art.mem 0.17 (but 84 of its 87 sit inside a VERBATIM\n63\thandback — an L-Prime pass there would destroy the \"verbatim\" claim), LEDGER 0.07 (127 total,\n64\tdominated by explanatory tails: \"which is\", \"is the\", \"is what\"), README/MIGRATION/CHANGELOG\n65\t0.04-0.06, contributing.md ZERO. Archaeology: the RECORD is far more evergreen than the harness\n66\tCOMMENTS; concentrations in gate-report.js:18-25 (a removed flag narrated in 8 lines),\n67\tcoverage-floor (13 of 24 lines narrating two re-seats), ruling-breadth-ceiling, must-fail.\n68\tFOUR stale present-tense counts that assert a blast radius and get it wrong: corpus-ledgers.test.js\n69\t\"Thirteen\" (