rectness; the 97-region population\n94\t   unconfirmed.\n95\tH. The debt backlogs: ablation-ledger 330 of 359 rows OWED, darkness-ledger 93 of 111. Whether these\n96\t   are enumerated backlogs or guards that stopped guarding decides the fate of the two largest corpus\n97\t   files. YIN did not read the 423 reasons.\n98\tI. syntaxes/attic SHIPS: .vscodeignore names no syntaxes/attic and package-contents checks manifest →\n99\t   package only, never package → needed, so a 14KB dead sketch grammar rides into every install.\n100\t   Inferred from source, NOT confirmed by building a .vsix.\n101\tJ. 63 `punctuation.separator` sites unread; either a fifth unstated naming law exists or it is accretion.\n102\t\n103\t## YIN's ranked collapse list (17 items, in order)\n104\t1 delete run_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test · 2 retire four narrowing test aliases ·\n105\t3 one `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()` · 4 the byte-identical helper and the inlined grammars.sh, AND\n106\tlift one-implementation's `.test.js` exclusion · 5 snap-tid + snap-meta · 6 drop the duplicate CI\n107\tcompose job · 7 one home for the migration headline (fixes two wrong 111s) · 8 derive 65 and BAR ·\n108\t9 generate the README gate list's completeness check, keep the curated prose · 10 fix the four stale\n109\tpresent-tense counts · 11 swallow-witness ⊂ still --over --reach (HIGHEST RISK; do not attempt\n110\twithout re-running both) · 12 three sentinels into one module · 13 corpus file naming to\n111\t-ledger/-ratchet with direction in the first comment · 14 MISS → dark/unmarked · 15 one lifecycle\n112\tvocabulary (idle/unruled/retired) · 16 move gate-report's archaeology paragraph into the LEDGER ·\n113\t17 keep syntaxes/attic out of the .vsix (verify by building one first).\n114\t"}]},"uuid":"18615286-b2fc-4aed-9bd3-6ec49fd5d688","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:32:20.088Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/trade/yin-wave1-for-yang.md","content":"# YIN