es its run set FROM package.json, so dropping a script entry\n20\t  retires that arm's exclusive rulings (31 and 57 by YANG's count).\n21\tA5 swallow-witness ⊂ still: STRUCK. Over the same corpus ground the two agree exactly —\n22\t  swallow's 13 classes sum to 186 instances (82+24+19+18+9+8+7+5+5+4+2+2+1) and still reports 186.\n23\t  The agreement is WHY they are two gates: still ratchets a coverage share (carrier-reach-floor) and\n24\t  a ruling-breadth bound; swallow alone produces unasked-regions-ceiling (97 regions carry no line\n25\t  bound, 83 open under some cut, 14 unasked) and an 18-region probe-escape reading. What survives:\n26\t  still.js:35-38 says the pass finds 8 classes; it finds 13 — a stale comment that caused YIN to rank\n27\t  a destructive collapse highest in wave one.\n28\tA6 the .vsix: CONFIRMED by observation (`vsce ls --no-dependencies`, 34 files). syntaxes/attic ships\n29\t  (sketch grammar 14,013 bytes + README 936). Larger than wave one saw: docs/prior-art ships too,\n30\t  seven design documents, 280,996 bytes; nine shipped .mem documents plus the attic total 349,604\n31\t  bytes. .vscodeignore names neither attic nor docs. package-contents.js:35-45 checks manifest →\n32\t  package only, never package → needed.\n33\t\n34\t## Reckonings\n35\tB1 One rule, two edits: every-gate-collides pairs a NAME match over RAW text with a CLAUSE match over\n36\t  comment-stripped code (lines 67/77), a GRAIN fault; one-implementation:33 excludes *.test.js, a\n37\t  POPULATION fault. corpus-ledgers.test.js:43 and :33-39 are the worked examples for both.\n38\t  Cost asymmetry: the first edit will red at least one currently-green gate; the second WIDENS\n39\t  obligations and needs a written allowance list.\n40\tB2 gate-report --check writes two tracked files: textmate-ceiling.js --write → TextMateCeiling.tid,\n41\t  and builtins-sync.js (no --check in the manifest) → syntaxes/tiddlywiki5.json, a SHIPPED grammar.\n42\t  Law that generalises: a harvest's CHECK arm belongs in the manifest, its WRITE arm never does.\n43\t  Precedent already correct twice: edition:build/edition:check and signals/signals:check.\n44\tB3 CI's \"not redundancy\" ruling covers the four previously-continue-on-error gates (signals:check,\n45\t  overreach-host, overreach-cut, upstream-coverage), NOT compose. The grammar job's apparent\n46\t  duplicates are defended by a four-way OS/node matrix; the compose job runs ubuntu/node22 — the same\n47\t  platform as gates. Platform coverage is the dividing line; compose is the only true duplicate job.\n48\tB4 Collision obligations: 21 of 39 invariants carry a recognised collider, 18 do not — and\n49\t  structurally NO invariant ever enters the pairing, since every-gate-collides pairs test files\n50\t  against GATE TOOL NAMES. The exemption is by construction and nothing records it.\n51\t  Items that move an obligation: the shared owedOf() (must carry delimiter-inheritance.test.js:104-107's\n52\t  collider across), lifting one-implementation's exclusion (adds obligations), fusing snap-tid+snap-meta\n53\t  (moves a denominator nobody publishes), the sentinel fusion (revised), the corpus renames, and the\n54\t  attic item — which must land with the first collider package-contents.js has ever had.\n55\t\n56\t## Wave-two list\n57\tCONFIRMED: delete run_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test (zero readers) · strike four narrowing test\n58\taliases (82 scripts → 75) · one owedOf() beside readerOf() (five ad-hoc /^OWED/ sites; bracket-witness\n59\tand light-cone do not strip the READER prefix; 76 live READER…OWED rows, all in darkness-ledger) ·\n60\ttwo edits for one rule (B1) · syntaxes/attic out of the package (C5, with a collider for\n61\tpackage-contents) · strike the CI compose job (B3) · one home for the migration headline, fixing two\n62\trestatements that say 111 where the certified figure is 110 (MIGRATION:36, SCOPE-NAMES:20) and noting\n63\tLEDGER:1294's drifted 585/122/247 · weld the theme count and derive BAR from it (five instruments\n64\thardcode node_modules/tm-themes with no override, so the weld must read \"65 as this repository\n65\tbundles them\") · fix four wrong present-tense counts (corpus-ledgers \"Thirteen\" vs 20, GateReport-Doc\n66\t\"Seventeen\" vs 49/35/65, theme-model.test \"Four gates\" vs 12 requirers, tokenizer.test \"Twenty-two\"\n67\tvs 26) without deleting the paragraphs · true still.js's 8 → 13 · MISS → dark/unmarked (one codec,\n68\ttwo ledgers, one homonym).\n69\tREVISED: share the two orphan sentinel STRINGS only, never the two baseline derivations (oracle\n70\treadAt vs a written control file — two of five containment grains) · generate the README's\n71\tcompleteness CHECK, keep the curated prose, put only a --check arm in the manifest (25 distinct names,\n72\t3 duplicated bullets, 37 of 49 gates unnamed, the weld asserting only existence) · move\n73\tgate-report.js:18-25's archaeology to LEDGER:1809-1812, which already holds it — a move, never a\n74\tdelete · snap-tid+snap-meta stays weakest-defended but do the collider fix first ·\n75\tcorpus file naming to -ledger/-ratchet with direction in the first comment line · one lifecycle\n76\tvocabulary (idle / unruled / retired), the winner already present in divergence-staleness:137.\n77\tSTRUCK: swallow ⊂ still · dark-construct ∪ contrast-witness · the overreach glob fusion ·\n78\tprose-reading-ledger ∪ PlainConstructs.\n79\t\n80\t## What YANG made visible to YIN\n81\tThe invariants' structural exemption from the collider requirement · package-contents as a blocking\n82\tuntested gate that C5 depends on · the 10 unused rulings being exactly the 10 READER 5.5.0-prerelease\n83\tones, keyed out by the same module owedOf() would extend, 4 of them OWED · flags that switch\n84\tPOPULATION rather than output, which withdraws all three \"one tool two gates\" candidates ·\n85\tbacktrack-witness's wall-clock sensitivity, which any item changing what-runs-beside-what can move ·\n86\tboth record welds reading the UNRELEASED section only, so new welds must key on something else.\n87\t\n88\t## Not verified this wave\n89\tNo gate-report --check (writes two tracked files) · no .vsix extraction (listing only) · no\n90\tstill --host --reach · no test-tools · the 63 punctuation.separator sites unread · the 423 OWED rows\n91\tunread (330 of 359 in ablation-ledger, 93 of 111 in darkness-ledger) — deciding whether those two\n92\tlargest corpus files are an enumerated backlog or a guard that stopped guarding · four of YANG's\n93\tseams not taken up: overreach-cut's 0 exclusives, canary-memetic vs memetic-containment, the four\n94\tcolour-reader CLI surfaces, the 6 invisible attic fixtures.\n95\t"}]},"uuid":"9b87e87d-4419-4715-8b49-df576d135792","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:32:21.461Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/trade/yin-wave2.md","content":"# YIN wave two (for the blind reader) — the seams, settled\nAll numbers are YIN's own measurements, stated with what they were measured over.\n\n## Measurements that settled a seam\nA1 dark-construct vs contrast-witness: 22 findings vs 26, UNION 47, INTERSECTION 1\n  (meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 only, and only because the two count different theme populations:\n  9 of 65 colour it, 12 of 65 reach-and-waste it). Structurally exclusive per theme — a scope cannot\n  be both unreached and reached-but-quiet in one theme. Fusing would lose 46 of 47 findings. KEEP BOTH.\n  What survives of YIN's wave-one claim: 2 lines of duplicated anecdote prose in two tool headers.\nA2 prose-reading-ledger (1 row) vs PlainConstructs.tid (20 keys): INTERSECTION 0. Both surfaces\n  exactly sized to their findings; neither carries a dead entry. Split by FAULT is right; split by\n  STORAGE (a corpus text file vs a JSON data tiddler, with colour-witness reading one of each) is\n  arbitrary.\nA3 carrier-ledger's 7 rows: `still --over ./corpus --reach` reads 52 of 52 carriers fully named,\n  100.0% (floor 99.5%), 186 divergences, 0 classes blocking — the corpus ledger was never consulted.\n  Consistent with its header's claim; not proof (wants the ~4403-carrier host sweep).\nA4 overreach's two glob arms: STRUCK. overreach-check.js:306 takes the FIRST non-flag argument as\n  the only pattern (handed to `bash -c \"ls …\"`), so two directories cannot be one glob;\n  divergence-staleness.js:48-51 derives its run set FROM package.json, so dropping a script entry\n  retires that arm's exclusive rulings (31 and 57 by YANG's count).\nA5 swallow-witness ⊂ still: STRUCK. Over the same corpus ground the two agree exactly —\n  swallow's 13 classes sum to 186 instances (82+24+19+18+9+8+7+5+5+4+2+2+1) and still reports 186.\n  The agreement is WHY they are two gates: still ratchets a coverage share (carrier-reach-floor) and\n  a ruling-breadth bound; swallow alone produces unasked-regions-ceiling (97 regions carry no line\n  bound, 83 open under some cut, 14 unasked) and an 18-region probe-escape reading. What survives:\n  still.js:35-38 says the pass finds 8 classes; it finds 13 — a stale comment that caused YIN to rank\n  a destructive collapse highest in wave one.\nA6 the .vsix: CONFIRMED by observation (`vsce ls --no-dependencies`, 34 files). syntaxes/attic ships\n  (sketch grammar 14,013 bytes + README 936). Larger than wave one saw: docs/prior-art ships too,\n  seven design documents, 280,996 bytes; nine shipped .mem documents plus the attic total 349,604\n  bytes. .vscodeignore names neither attic nor docs. package-contents.js:35-45 checks manifest →\n  package only, never package → needed.\n\n## Reckonings\nB1 One rule, two edits: every-gate-collides pairs a NAME match over RAW text with a CLAUSE match over\n  comment-stripped code (lines 67/77), a GRAIN fault; one-implementation:33 excludes *.test.js, a\n  POPULATION fault. corpus-ledgers.test.js:43 and :33-39 are the worked examples for both.\n  Cost asymmetry: the first edit will red at least one currently-green gate; the second WIDENS\n  obligations and needs a written allowance list.\nB2 gate-report --check writes two tracked files: textmate-ceiling.js --write → TextMateCeiling.tid,\n  and builtins-sync.js (no --check in the manifest) → syntaxes/tiddlywiki5.json, a SHIPPED grammar.\n  Law that generalises: a harvest's CHECK arm belongs in the manifest, its WRITE arm never does.\n  Precedent already correct twice: edition:build/edition:check and signals/signals:check.\nB3 CI's \"not redundancy\" ruling covers the four previously-continue-on-error gates (signals:check,\n  overreach-host, overreach-cut, upstream-coverage), NOT compose. The grammar job's apparent\n  duplicates are defended by a four-way OS/node matrix; the compose job runs ubuntu/node22 — the same\n  platform as gates. Platform coverage is the dividing line; compose is the only true duplicate job.\nB4 Collision obligations: 21 of 39 invariants carry a recognised collider, 18 do not — and\n  structurally NO invariant ever enters the pairing, since every-gate-collides pairs test files\n  against GATE TOOL NAMES. The exemption is by construction and nothing records it.\n  Items that move an obligation: the shared owedOf() (must carry delimiter-inheritance.test.js:104-107's\n  collider across), lifting one-implementation's exclusion (adds obligations), fusing snap-tid+snap-meta\n  (moves a denominator nobody publishes), the sentinel fusion (revised), the corpus renames, and the\n  attic item — which must land with the first collider package-contents.js has ever had.\n\n## Wave-two list\nCONFIRMED: delete run_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test (zero readers) · strike four narrowing test\naliases (82 scripts → 75) · one owedOf() beside readerOf() (five ad-hoc /^OWED/ sites; bracket-witness\nand light-cone do not strip the READER prefix; 76 live READER…OWED rows, all in darkness-ledger) ·\ntwo edits for one rule (B1) · syntaxes/attic out of the package (C5, with a collider for\npackage-contents) · strike the CI compose job (B3) · one home for the migration headline, fixing two\nrestatements that say 111 where the certified figure is 110 (MIGRATION:36, SCOPE-NAMES:20) and noting\nLEDGER:1294's drifted 585/122/247 · weld the theme count and derive BAR from it (five instruments\nhardcode node_modules/tm-themes with no override, so the weld must read \"65 as this repository\nbundles them\") · fix four wrong present-tense counts (corpus-ledgers \"Thirteen\" vs 20, GateReport-Doc\n\"Seventeen\" vs 49/35/65, theme-model.test \"Four gates\" vs 12 requirers, tokenizer.test \"Twenty-two\"\nvs 26) without deleting the paragraphs · true still.js's 8 → 13 · MISS → dark/unmarked (one codec,\ntwo ledgers, one homonym).\nREVISED: share the two orphan sentinel STRINGS only, never the two baseline derivations (oracle\nreadAt vs a written control file — two of five containment grains) · generate the README's\ncompleteness CHECK, keep the curated prose, put only a --check arm in the manifest (25 distinct names,\n3 duplicated bullets, 37 of 49 gates unnamed, the weld asserting only existence) · move\ngate-report.js:18-25's archaeology to LEDGER:1809-1812, which already holds it — a move, never a\ndelete · snap-tid+snap-meta stays weakest-defended but do the collider fix first ·\ncorpus file naming to -ledger/-ratchet with direction in the first comment line · one lifecycle\nvocabulary (idle / unruled / retired), the winner already present in divergence-staleness:137.\nSTRUCK: swallow ⊂ still · dark-construct ∪ contrast-witness · the overreach glob fusion ·\nprose-reading-ledger ∪ PlainConstructs.\n\n## What YANG made visible to YIN\nThe invariants' structural exemption from the collider requirement · package-contents as a blocking\nuntested gate that C5 depends on · the 10 unused rulings being exactly the 10 READER 5.5.0-prerelease\nones, keyed out by the same module owedOf() would extend, 4 of them OWED · flags that switch\nPOPULATION rather than output, which withdraws all three \"one tool two gates\" candidates ·\nbacktrack-witness's wall-clock sensitivity, which any item changing what-runs-beside-what can move ·\nboth record welds reading the UNRELEASED section only, so new welds must key on something else.\n\n## Not verified this wave\nNo gate-report --check (writes two tracked files) · no .vsix extraction (listing only) · no\nstill --host --reach · no test-tools · the 63 punctuation.separator sites unread · the 423 OWED rows\nunread (330 of 359 in ablation-ledger, 93 of 111 in darkness-ledger) — deciding whether those two\nlargest corpus files are an enumerated backlog or a guard that stopped guarding · four of YANG's\nseams not taken up: overreach-cut's 0 exclusives, canary-memetic vs memetic-containment, the four\ncolour-reader CLI surfaces, the 6 invisible attic fixtures.\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d19cbf6-cddf-4038-9616-34725eecb1d7","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/VSCode-TW5-Syntax","sessionId":"7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9","version":"2.1.277","gitBranch":"release/3.0.0","slug":"luminous-strolling-torvalds"}
./packages/lararium-sensorium/fixtures/claude-week-2026-10-07/sources/claude/7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9/subagents/agent-a876d2adbe9a4390a.jsonl:21:{"parentUuid":"3602bbc2-e943-401f-889e-65913be155c3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a474019c-acfa-471e-8c33-89e46680e0d2","agentId":"a876d2adbe9a4390a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QvqcRASzjv8oxbsEAqqrJw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# YANG wave two (for the blind reader) — rulings, defences, concessions\n2\tAll numbers are YANG's own measurements, stated with what they were measured over.\n3\t\n4\t## A1 The fixtures: vocabulary is the wrong measure\n5\tMeasured 60 of 87 fixtures whose asserted scope VOCABULARY is contained in the 737 distinct scopes the\n6\t40 snapshots carry (YIN measured 50 by a narrower extraction; both agree on the property).\n7\tTwo properties defeat vocabulary subsumption:\n8\t (i) NEGATIVE assertions — 36 of 87 fixtures carry them, 138 in total; the snapshot format records\n9\t     what IS present and has no syntax for absence. 29 of the 60 carry negatives → categorically\n10\t     un-snapshotable.\n11\t (ii) CONSTRUCT presence ≠ vocabulary presence. `macro-dynamic-params` pins 76 assertions over seven\n12\t     parameter-value forms; SIX of the seven appear in ZERO snapshot samples (filtered `{{{}}}`,\n13\t     indirect `{{t!!f}}`, mvv `((v))`, backtick and triple-backtick substitution, nested call), and\n14\t     three appear in zero broad-corpus files either, so no coverage or overreach gate reads them. One\n15\t     of them sits under a live OWED ruling. YANG self-corrected one earlier claim: `macro-string-params`\n16\t     IS snapshot-covered (samples carry 14 named-argument calls).\n17\tRULING: of the 60, 56 pin a LAW — 29 by negative assertion, 22 by explanatory prose, 4 by a law stated\n18\tin the fixture's own header line. FOUR are behaviour-only and fusible (`blockquote`,\n19\t`macro-string-params`, `mvv-display`, `pragma-params-mvv`, 127 assertion lines between them).\n20\t`macro-dynamic-params` DEFENDED on construct absence. One header description is simply wrong\n21\t(`blockquote` says \"Test for header syntaxes\").\n22\t\n23\t## A2 The colour cluster: the load-bearing claim confirmed, the integers not reproducible\n24\tContainer claim CONFIRMED and strengthened: across the 65 bundled themes, rules reaching\n25\t`meta.variable.call` 0/65, `meta.transclusion` 0/65, `meta.variable` 2/65, `meta` 65/65 — and the\n26\tcontainer stacks of a call, a filter run, a transclusion and prose resolve IDENTICALLY in 65 of 65\n27\t(the tool's own header says 44 of 65; YANG's reading is harsher). A container-grain legibility gate\n28\twould be worthless; the distinction rides on the punctuation and name scopes inside.\n29\tQuiet-rule derivation CONFIRMED in rank and ratio: 1,467 quiet of 15,116 foreground rule-parts = 9.7%\n30\t(header: 1,191 of 11,756 = 10.1%); `variable` ranks first, quiet in 23 of the 59 themes that rule it\n31\t= 39% (header: 18 of 54 = 33%). Runners-up: variable.other 23/43, string 18/62, meta.embedded 17/23,\n32\tmarkup.bold 11/55, markup.italic 11/46. YANG reports one broken probe it corrected mid-measurement.\n33\tShared anecdote: one event in three headers; the three MECHANISMS differ (absent rule / rule within\n34\tCIE76 ΔE of the theme default / below the median of six comparator grammars). CONDITIONAL: one home\n35\tfor the anecdote, three gates stay.\n36\tFINDING: none of the three header integers reproduces exactly from the shipped modules, though all\n37\treproduce in rank, direction and ratio — so the HARNESS's doc-comment integers are dated readings in\n38\tthe present tense, the same defect as the RECORD's figures. One defect, not two.\n39\t\n40\t## A3 The /^OWED/ divergence: LATENT, and sharper than YIN stated\n41\tSix sites test the OWED prefix; three strip `READER <version>` first via the shared reader\n42\t(ablation-witness:361, darkness-witness:219, swallow-witness:107-108), three do NOT\n43\t(light-cone:81, bracket-witness:155, delimiter-inheritance.test:96,106). Neither light-cone nor\n44\tbracket-witness imports the reader-scope module.\n45\tSHARPER: light-cone and swallow-witness read THE SAME FILE (swallow-ledger.txt) with incompatible\n46\tpredicates — no second file is needed for the fault.\n47\tDistribution corrected: the 76 `READER <v> OWED` rows are 65 in darkness-ledger, 7 in\n48\tablation-ledger, 4 in expected-divergence — all three read by stripping readers, so all 76 are handled\n49\ttoday. swallow-ledger carries five READER rows and zero OWED; adding OWED to any ONE of them makes it\n50\tlive immediately.\n51\tCONSEQUENCE: light-cone's gate is one-sided by design — it refuses only rows filed OWED. A\n52\t`READER 5.4.1 OWED` row reads to it as RULED, moving it out of the refusable set, so the gate CANNOT\n53\tGO RED on that row. It does not disagree loudly; it goes silent. YANG promotes this to FIRST on either\n54\tlist — the only latent fault that disarms a gate.\n55\t\n56\t## A4 The ward's blind spot: lifting the exclusion is UNSAFE\n57\tone-implementation builds two populations; only the FINGERPRINT scan excludes `*.test.js`. Four other\n58\tchecks in the same file already reach into tests, via a NAMED five-entry exemption map. The exclusion\n59\tcarries its reason two lines above it: a test sits beside the instrument it collides, and holding a\n60\ttest to the no-second-implementation rule would FORBID the collision the house requires.\n61\tRULING: CONDITIONAL — keep the exclusion, extend the existing named-exemption mechanism to the\n62\tfingerprint scan.\n63\tDuplications measured: the byte-identical `scopesOn` helper exists in exactly TWO invariants (YIN's\n64\tcount right); a THIRD file carries a function of the same name that is a different function\n65\t(offset-based, returns an array) — a legibility hazard nothing reads. `source ./grammars.sh` is\n66\tinlined ONCE, not twice (the second file YIN named reads grammars.sh as a file, a different act).\n67\tSo lifting the exclusion surfaces two real duplications — both fixable today without touching the ward.\n68\t\n69\t## A5 The debt backlogs: CONCEDED, with a structural condition\n70\tRead EVERY owed reason in both files (not a sample). ablation-ledger: 359 rows, 319 OWED, **22 distinct\n71\treason bodies**, distinct stems also 22 — byte-identical repeats, largest family 96 rows (a style run's\n72\t`;`/`:` separators), then 40, 38, 38, 23, 18, 14, 10. darkness-ledger: 111 rows, 92 OWED, **5 distinct\n73\tbodies**, 3 distinct stems, largest family 89 rows (a filter or template-title value spanning a blank\n74\tline) — and that cause is stated a second time in the file's own header.\n75\tRULING: these are not 319 and 92 guards; they are 22 and 5 causes enumerated at the row granularity the\n76\tkey grammar forces (one row per character position).\n77\tCONDITION, non-negotiable: a single-number ratchet seated at 1 refuses a ruling absorbing more than one\n78\tcause, and its header records why — a predecessor ratchet on corpus-token share re-seated four times in\n79\tone session (55.8 → 56.6 → 57.2 → 60.0%), every reason true, because authoring more of what is already\n80\truled raises the share. So the collapse is safe ONLY once the ledger row grammar carries a `cause`\n81\tidentifier distinct from its `key` and the breadth ratchet counts distinct causes rather than keys.\n82\tThen ~400 lines of verbatim repetition leave the two largest ledgers and nothing is lost — the single\n83\tlargest honest reduction on either list.\n84\t\n85\t## Part B verdicts on YIN's candidates\n86\tsnap-tid + snap-meta — CONCEDE, nothing lost (2 and 1 sample files; a different invariant holds the\n87\tfile associations).\n88\toverreach-cut — CONDITIONAL, and the condition is CI, not the gate: `degraded-ground.test.js` runs the\n89\tcut arm itself with a byte-identical invocation, but it SKIPS unless a TiddlyWiki checkout sits as a\n90\tSIBLING of the repository — true on the operator's machine, false in CI. So in CI the gate is the only\n91\treader of degraded ground. Fix the test's host resolution first, then the gate can go.\n92\tengine-witness / engine-behaviour — DEFEND (a compile is not an agreement; the engine ledger's single\n93\truling is BEHAVIOUR-prefixed and filtered out of the compile arm).\n94\tstill / still-reach — DEFEND (sampled vs whole; the carrier floor seated at 0.9947; 23 of 4,403\n95\tcarriers hold an unnamed class so a draw of 25 misses all 23 seven times in eight; seeds 1/2/9/13 green\n96\tand seed 5 red off one unchanged tree).\n97\tThe harvest's per-arm summary line is HABIT: the report counts what the manifest names and no file\n98\tstates 49.\n99\trun_snapshots.sh + echo-test + list-test — CONCEDE all three, with a coupling: run_snapshots.sh is\n100\treferenced once more, by `.vscodeignore:16`, and the package gate checks manifest→package only, so a\n101\tstale ignore entry would go unreported. Delete both lines together.\n102\tThe four stale present-tense counts — ALL FOUR CONFIRMED: theme-model's \"Four gates\" against 12\n103\tnon-test readers (8 of them gates, 18 requirers total); tokenizer's \"Twenty-two\" against 26 non-test\n104\t(35 total); the doc tiddler's \"Seventeen instruments\" against 49 gates over 35 instruments — while the\n105\ttool's own header refuses to state a count; the corpus-ledger invariant's \"Thirteen\" against 20.\n106\t\n107\t## Part C — YANG's verdict over YIN's 17, plus ordering\n108\tCONCEDE: 1, 2, 3 (promoted to FIRST), 4a, 5, 6, 7 (a correctness fix — two restatements say 111 where\n109\tthe certified figure is 110, and one file contradicts itself 31 lines apart), 8 (and WIDEN), 9, 10,\n110\t12 (strings only), 13, 14, 15.\n111\tDEFEND / CONDITIONAL: 4b (decline as written; extend the exemption map instead), 11 (defend — the\n112\tswallow witness alone computes a coverage ceiling seated at 14 over a population of 97 regions, with\n113\t83 standing open under some cut and agreeing with the host; adding 800 upstream carriers opens twelve\n114\tmore), 16 (move, never lose — and carry the reader-keyed report routing note with it, which no test\n115\tholds), 17 (verify by building a .vsix first; same missing package→needed direction as item 1).\n116\tYANG's own items YIN did not touch: the collider invariant's false green (name matched in a comment,\n117\tclause matched elsewhere; the real collider is excellent and invisible — one-line fix, strip comments\n118\tbefore the name match); two of the 49 gates writing tracked files so the report is not read-only;\n119\tfour CI-blocking instruments outside the collider requirement, one with no test at all; nothing\n120\tcollides the 39 invariants and no ruling says why; the deliberate absences (the within-construct\n121\twitness, the unarticulated fragment) and the two throwaway scouts that are the only implementation of\n122\tthe continuity reading — all of which look exactly like gaps and dead code and are neither.\n123\t\n124\t## THE BLIND SPOT YIN MADE VISIBLE TO YANG\n125\tThe record and the harness have NO SYNTAX for \"this number was true when measured\" versus \"this number\n126\tis true now\", and every staleness finding in both reports is downstream of that one absence. Arrived at\n127\tfrom four directions: a ledger row stating 585/122/247 against the certified 556/110/245 while\n128\tnarrating a sequence; two restatements saying 111 for 110 in welded files in shapes the weld's patterns\n129\tdo not match; 106 figures of N-of-65 or a percentage in the welded section with ZERO read by anything\n130\tand only 6 machine-readable twins in the whole repository; and three harness doc-comment derivations\n131\tthat reproduce in rank and ratio but not in integer.\n132\tCURE, one mark: a dated reading carries its date, a live claim carries a machine-readable twin, and a\n133\tfigure carrying neither fails its gate. That single distinction retires YIN's items 7, 8 and 10 and\n134\tYANG's wave-one staleness class at once — the only item on either list that pays for itself across\n135\tboth the record and the harness.\n136\t\n137\t## Ordering advice\n138\tItem 3 first (the only latent fault that disarms a gate). The dated-reading mark second (retires four\n139\titems). Then 1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 10, 13, 14, 15, 4a freely. Hold 11 and 17 for measurement. Decline 4b as\n140\twritten.\n141\t\n142\t## Not verified\n143\tNo .vsix built · no gate report, tool suite, backtrack, snapshot, canary or theme gate run (gates\n144\tactually run across both waves: the five overreach arms and divergence-staleness) · three doc-comment\n145\tintegers not reproducible (claimed only as not-reproducible, not as wrong) · two OWED counting methods\n146\tdiffer (330/93 by line grep, 319/92 by reason-splitting; the distinct-reason counts 22 and 5 are robust\n147\tto that) · YIN's attic fixture count (7 vs 6), node:test declaration counts, copula densities and the\n148\ttwo sandbox probe claims unverified.\n149\t"}]},"uuid":"b17dc759-4833-4f94-8f84-bf353452f959","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:32:22.102Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/trade/yang-wave2.md","content":"# YANG wave two (for the blind reader) — rulings, defences, concessions\nAll numbers are YANG's own measurements, stated with what they were measured over.\n\n## A1 The fixtures: vocabulary is the wrong measure\nMeasured 60 of 87 fixtures whose asserted scope VOCABULARY is contained in the 737 distinct scopes the\n40 snapshots carry (YIN measured 50 by a narrower extraction; both agree on the property).\nTwo properties defeat vocabulary subsumption:\n (i) NEGATIVE assertions — 36 of 87 fixtures carry them, 138 in total; the snapshot format records\n     what IS present and has no syntax for absence. 29 of the 60 carry negatives → categorically\n     un-snapshotable.\n (ii) CONSTRUCT presence ≠ vocabulary presence. `macro-dynamic-params` pin