le within\nCIE76 ΔE of the theme default / below the median of six comparator grammars). CONDITIONAL: one home\nfor the anecdote, three gates stay.\nFINDING: none of the three header integers reproduces exactly from the shipped modules, though all\nreproduce in rank, direction and ratio — so the HARNESS's doc-comment integers are dated readings in\nthe present tense, the same defect as the RECORD's figures. One defect, not two.\n\n## A3 The /^OWED/ divergence: LATENT, and sharper than YIN stated\nSix sites test the OWED prefix; three strip `READER <version>` first via the shared reader\n(ablation-witness:361, darkness-witness:219, swallow-witness:107-108), three do NOT\n(light-cone:81, bracket-witness:155, delimiter-inheritance.test:96,106). Neither light-cone nor\nbracket-witness imports the reader-scope module.\nSHARPER: light-cone and swallow-witness read THE SAME FILE (swallow-ledger.txt) with incompatible\npredicates — no second file is needed for the fault.\nDistribution corrected: the 76 `READER <v> OWED` rows are 65 in darkness-ledger, 7 in\nablation-ledger, 4 in expected-divergence — all three read by stripping readers, so all 76 are handled\ntoday. swallow-ledger carries five READER rows and zero OWED; adding OWED to any ONE of them makes it\nlive immediately.\nCONSEQUENCE: light-cone's gate is one-sided by design — it refuses only rows filed OWED. A\n`READER 5.4.1 OWED` row reads to it as RULED, moving it out of the refusable set, so the gate CANNOT\nGO RED on that row. It does not disagree loudly; it goes silent. YANG promotes this to FIRST on either\nlist — the only latent fault that disarms a gate.\n\n## A4 The ward's blind spot: lifting the exclusion is UNSAFE\none-implementation builds two populations; only the FINGERPRINT scan excludes `*.test.js`. Four other\nchecks in the same file already reach into tests, via a NAMED five-entry exemption map. The exclusion\ncarries its reason two lines above it: a test sits beside the instrument it collides, and