te list: 25 names, 3 duplicate bullets, 37 of 49 unnamed, weld checks existence only (YIN R6). Four wrong counts (all confirmed by YANG): \"Thirteen\" (20), \"Seventeen instruments\" (49/35/65), \"Four gates\" (8 gates / 12 non-test readers / 18 requirers), \"Twenty-two\" (26 non-test / 35). Three colour header integers reproduce in rank/ratio, not integer (YANG A2). ONE SHAPE: a figure is dated or derived — the mark.\n\n**Q11. What ships?** `.vscodeignore`, `package-contents.js` (manifest→package only). `vsce ls`: 34 files; syntaxes/attic 14,013+936 bytes; docs/prior-art seven documents 280,996 bytes; nine .mem + attic 349,604 bytes (YIN A6, listing only). `.vscodeignore:16` references run_snapshots.sh (YANG).\n\n**Q12. Does the grammar stall?** backtrack-witness — wall-clock: 1.4 ms alone vs past 8 ms under the suite; 0 vs 6 stalls at rest (YANG). Keep; re-measure after every phase that changes what runs beside it.\n\n## B. The ordered plan\n\n### Phase 0 — make the verifier honest\n**0.1** every-gate-collides strips comments before the NAME match. Lost: nothing; at least one green gate will red (YIN B1) — that red is the finding. Evidence: YANG fault 1; corpus-ledgers.test.js:43 is the worked example. Why before step 1: every later move/delete of a test file is certified by this invariant, and step 1 must carry delimiter-inheritance.test.js:104-107's collider across (YIN B3).\n**0.2** the manifest names only --check arms (`ceiling` → textmate-ceiling.js --check; `builtins` → builtins-sync.js --check). Evidence: YANG fault 2; YIN B2's law and precedents (edition:build/check, signals/signals:check). The hand runs `gate-report --check` after every phase; today that dirties the tree twice.\n**0.3** write the exemption down: invariants enter no collider pairing by construction; the four CI gates outside the invariant listed by name. Evidence: YANG 4–5, YIN B4.\n\n### Phase 1 — the one latent fault that disarms a gate\n**1.1** one `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()`; six sites call it. Lost: nothing today (all 76 rows sit in stripping readers, YANG 65/7/4). First: 0.1. Evidence: YANG A3 — light-cone and swallow-witness read the SAME file with incompatible predicates; swallow-ledger holds five READER rows, zero OWED; add OWED to one and light-cone's one-sided gate reads it RULED and goes silent. Collider: a `READER 5.4.1 OWED` row in a sandboxed swallow-ledger must red light-cone after and be shown green-by-silence before.\n**Do I agree with \"first\"?** On substance yes: it precedes every collapse, since every ledger rename (phase 4) and the backlog re-key (C4) passes through this reader, and a re-key through six divergent predicates is six faults. On the literal position no: phase 0 is what makes 1.1's verification trustworthy and costs three lines. If the hand can take one step only, take 1.1.\n\n### Phase 2 — pure removals\n**2.1** delete `run_snapshots.sh` + `echo-test` + `list-test` AND `.vscodeignore:16` together (YANG's coupling: the package gate never reports a stale ignore entry).\n**2.2** strike the four narrowing aliases (82 → 75, YIN). First: F.1.\n**2.3** strike CI `compose`. Must NOT touch test.yml:88-95 or the matrix.\n**2.4** fuse snap-tid + snap-meta. Lost: a harvest summary line — YANG: habit, no file states 49. First: 0.1 and F.3.\n**2.5** `scopesOn` ×2 → tokenizer.js's helper; the one inlined `source ./grammars.sh` → the shared act; rename the third same-named different function (YANG A4). No ward change needed.\n**2.6** share the three sentinel STRINGS; keep both baseline derivations.\n\n### Phase 3 — the mark, then every figure under it\n**3.1** ONE syntax for a figure: `<figure> (read <date>, over <population>)` or a machine twin — reuse the `# checks:` form already in 6 places, never a second. ONE gate: a figure in a welded file carrying neither fails; keyed on the mark, NOT on UNRELEASED (both existing welds go blind when 3.1.0 opens — YANG). Position: after phases 1–2 so derived figures describe the collapsed tree; before 3.2–3.8 so each fix is an instance of the mark. YANG wanted it second; the only difference is letting the pure removals go first because they change counts the mark would otherwise date twice.\n**3.2** one home for the migration headline; MIGRATION:36 and SCOPE-NAMES:20 111→110; LEDGER:1294's 585/122/247 marked as the dated sequence it narrates, not corrected; three regexes → one weld on the mark. Caution F.2 (110 vs 111) before editing.\n**3.3** weld the theme count (\"65 as this repository bundles them\"); derive BAR from it.\n**3.4** fix the four counts WITHOUT deleting paragraphs — each derived or dated, population named.\n**3.5** still.js:35-38 8 → 13, dated.\n**3.6** the three colour header integers get date and population; do NOT overwrite with YANG's re-run (C5). Anecdote to ONE home; each header keeps one line naming its MECHANISM.\n**3.7** generate the README gate list's completeness CHECK; keep curated prose; --check arm only in the manifest.\n**3.8** move gate-report.js:18-25 to LEDGER:1809-1812 (already holds it); carry 38-46's routing LAW into the LEDGER while LEAVING the comment in place (no test holds it).\n\n### Phase 4 — vocabulary (after phase 1; every rename passes through owedOf/readerOf and ledger-shape)\n**4.1** `-ledger`/`-ratchet` names, direction in the first comment line (confirm `attribute-kind-ceiling` first, F.6); collider obligations move with names. **4.2** `MISS` → `dark`/`unmarked`. **4.3** `idle`/`unruled`/`retired`. **4.4** one spelling of overreach (YIN V2), weld-grep first.\n\n### Phase 5 — conditionals\n**5.1** attic (and docs/prior-art) out of the .vsix: build AND EXTRACT first; land with package-contents' first collider; add package→needed. Attic stays in the tree. **5.2** retire overreach-cut: C3. **5.3** backlog collapse: C4. **5.4** fuse the four behaviour-only fixtures once each has a snapshot sample; fix `blockquote`'s wrong header regardless. **5.5** one home for judgements (corpus text vs JSON tiddlers): record the axis per surface; move no data until read. **5.6** four colour CLI surfaces — HELD. **5.7** canary-memetic vs memetic-containment — HELD.\n\n### Phase 6 — L-Prime / Evergreen, once (D).\n\n## C. Adjudications\n\n**C1 Fixtures (50 vs 60; subsumption).** Vocabulary subsumption is NOT safe; the 50/60 gap is irrelevant. Follow YANG: 36 of 87 carry 138 negatives and snapshots have no absence syntax (29 of the 60 lost outright); construct presence ≠ vocabulary presence (six of seven macro-dynamic-params forms in zero snapshots, one under live OWED). YIN itself handed the law question over. 4 fusible, 83 stay. Would change it: an absence-recording snapshot format AND a scope-at-position measurement — both, not either.\n\n**C2 The ward's `.test.js` exclusion.** Keep it; extend the existing five-entry named-exemption map to the fingerprint scan (YANG A4). The reason two lines above the exclusion is decisive: a test must hold its gate's collider, and the no-second-implementation rule on tests would forbid the collision the house requires. Lifting widens obligations (YIN B1 concedes). The two duplications are fixed in 2.5 without the ward. Would change it: the map cannot express \"a test may carry its collided instrument's body\" — then a new map entry kind, still no blanket lift.\n\n**C3 overreach-cut.** YANG's condition, YANG's order: fix degraded-ground.test.js's host resolution so it RUNS in CI (today it skips unless a TW checkout is a sibling; a skip reads as a pass), confirm a run not a skip, then drop the script — and re-confirm 0 exclusives at that moment (it is a property of the current ruling file, not of the arm; divergence-staleness derives from package.json). Would change it: a non-zero exclusive after the fix, or no way to give CI a host.\n\n**C4 Backlogs and the one-cause ratchet.** YANG's concession, YANG's condition, non-negotiable: `cause` identifier distinct from `key`; breadth ratchet counts causes; ratchet seated at 1 refuses a ruling absorbing more than one cause, header stating why (predecessor re-seated 55.8→56.6→57.2→60.0% in one session, every reason true). 22 and 5 causes at character-position grain forced by the key grammar (darkness's 89-row cause is restated in its own header). 330/93 vs 319/92 is method; untouched. Order: after phase 1 and 4.1. Would change it: a row-grain reader nobody named.\n\n**C5 Colour header integers.** Dated readings in the present tense — \"one defect, not two\" (YANG). Rank/direction/ratio reproduce (variable first both times; 9.7% vs 10.1%); integers and populations moved (59 vs 54 themes; 15,116 vs 11,756). Do not rewrite 44→65; date the 44 with its population, or replace with a derivation producing a machine twin. Three gates stay (fusion loses 46 of 47 findings, YIN). Would change it: a shipped derivation script — then no integer in the header at all.\n\n**Closed by the poles, do not reopen:** swallow ⊂ still; dark-construct ∪ contrast-witness; the overreach glob fusion; prose-reading-ledger ∪ PlainConstructs; the three flag-pairs as \"one tool two gates\" (flags switch POPULATION, YANG; YIN accepts).\n\n## D. Evergreen / L-Prime, as work (densities are YIN's; YANG did not verify)\n\n**Touches, by yield:** (1) harness comment archaeology — gate-report.js:18-25 (moved in 3.8); coverage-floor's header (13 of 24 lines narrate two re-seats → one dated line, history to the LEDGER); ruling-breadth-ceiling and must-fail headers. (2) LEDGER: 127 copulas at 0.07/line, explanatory tails (\"which is\", \"is the\", \"is what\") — turn the tails; copulas stating a ruling stay with a confidence marker; the 106 figures go through the mark, not prose. (3) README/MIGRATION/CHANGELOG at 0.04–0.06 — CHANGELOG's past entries are dated by construction, touch only UNRELEASED; MIGRATION sentences a weld reads change only WITH the weld. (4) the four count paragraphs — number fixed under the mark, sentence turned to say what the count GUARDS.\n\n**Must not touch:** docs/scope-naming-prior-art.mem — 84 of 87 copulas inside a VERBATIM handback; only the 3 outside are in scope. contributing.md — zero copulas. The 19 load-bearing sites (E): rephrase in place, never move/shorten/delete unless the law is first carried into a test or LEDGER row. Any weld-read sentence. Quoted error strings, operator-spoken rulings, fixture header lines stating a law (4, YANG).\n\n**Three questions per sentence:** (1) inside a fence/quotation/verbatim block? leave it. (2) does an instrument read it? change only with that reader, red first. (3) does it state a law nothing else holds? keep content word-for-word, turn only the copula, never move it alone. Three no's → turn freely: name what it does, date any number, derive any count.\n\n## E. Refused from any tidy-up (thing · why it looks removable · read first)\n- LEDGER:856-861 within-construct witness DEFERRED BY RULING · 851-855 fragment unarticulated on purpose · 780-790 underline one stroke · 836-850 two REFUSED palette moves.\n- uri-span-measure / uri-span-compare — the ONLY implementation of the continuity reading, cited for the underline ruling (YANG).\n- still-breadth.js, tw5-oracle-path.js — child processes in swapped-grammar sandboxes (YIN).\n- The shared modules (sentinel, region-kind, carrier-reading, ledger-shape, walk, jsonc, tokenizer, run-tool) — RESULTS of earlier collapses; one-implementation catches re-expansion, not wrong fusion.\n- Both attic READMEs and the 6/7 attic fixtures — invisible to every glob BY DESIGN; may leave the package, never the tree.\n- CI test.yml:88-95 (four re-runs = blocking) and :60-69 (dirty-tree reason).\n- gate-report.js:38-46 routing (no test holds it); its SKIP regex (change only with the reasons list, F.5).\n- The 10 `READER 5.5.0-prerelease` rulings — keyed out, 4 OWED, not stale.\n- overreach-corpus-memetic's 2 exclusives (the dialect's readability); engine-ledger's one BEHAVIOUR ruling; carrier-ledger's refusing header; macro-dynamic-params.\n- backtrack-witness.test.js:48-66; a-lar-uri-reads-without-underline header; corpus-ledgers.test.js header (fix the number, keep the law); coverage-floor, ruling-breadth-ceiling, carrier-reach-floor, legibility-floor, colour-pair-ledger headers; delimiter-inheritance.test.js:104-107.\n- Conditional skips — never convert a skip into deletion of the gate it stands for.\n- The two containment baselines; the three colour mechanism lines.\n\n## F. Unmeasured, and what settles it\n1. What runs the 96 fixtures (every-test-runs sees none). Before 2.2: diff each alias's population against the umbrella script's.\n2. 110 (YIN certified) vs 111 rulings in expected-divergence (YANG) — same thing? One grep of what the weld certifies. Before 3.2.\n3. Whether any file states \"49\" (YIN \"49 of 49\" vs YANG \"no file states 49\"). Before 2.4/5.2.\n4. `still --host --reach` over ~4,403 carriers — settles carrier-ledger's 7 rows.\n5. SKIP regex vs reasons list — which names the four outside CI gates. Before 0.3.\n6. attribute-kind-ceiling's comparator direction. Before 4.1.\n7. The 63 punctuation.separator sites — fifth naming law or accretion. Out of scope until read.\n8. backtrack-witness under the collapsed suite — re-measure after phases 2 and 5.\n9. What reads the 6 `# checks:` twins — the mark must reuse it, not add a second reader.\n10. A .vsix extracted, not listed — settles 5.1.\n11. The four CLI colour surfaces and canary-memetic — held until read.\n12. Copula densities — YIN's only; a second count before phase 6 is cheap.\n\n## G. Short form\n0. Collider strips comments before the name match · manifest names only --check arms · write the invariants' exemption down.\n1. `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()`, six sites, collider carried, red-first on a sandboxed swallow-ledger.\n2. Three dead scripts + `.vscodeignore:16` · four aliases (after F.1) · CI compose · snap-tid/snap-meta · two duplications + one misnamed function · three sentinel strings.\n3. The dated-or-derived mark with one gate keyed on it · then headline/110 (after F.2), theme count + BAR, four counts, 8→13, colour integers dated, README check generated, gate-report archaeology moved.\n4. `-ledger`/`-ratchet` with direction · MISS → dark/unmarked · idle/unruled/retired · one spelling of overreach.\n5. Conditionals behind their conditions: attic out of the .vsix with package-contents' first collider · overreach-cut after degraded-ground runs in CI · backlogs after the cause field and one-cause ratchet · four fixtures after their samples exist.\n6. L-Prime/Evergreen once, with D's three questions, never inside the verbatim handback."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16170,"cache_read_input_tokens":64683,"output_tokens":9954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":59},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16170},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":9954,"cache_read_input_tokens":64683,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16170,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LjGH8R24htp3yfgT1VLBdd":{"message":"Consolidation plan saved to `/home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/fable/consolidation-plan.md`. Nothing in the repository was read, run, or edited; the plan stands on the four survey files alone. Full text follows.\n\n---\n\n# Consolidation plan — VSCode-TW5-Syntax harness and record\n\nWritten blind, from four survey files only. Every number below belongs to the pole that measured it (YIN or YANG, wave 1 or 2); where I write no attribution, the two poles agree. I have not read the repository and I invent no figure. Where a step depends on a measurement nobody took, the step says so and section F names what would settle it.\n\n## 0. The four goals, kept apart\n\n| Goal | What it means here | Where it lands |\n|---|---|---|\n| Isomorphic by intent | one shape per QUESTION; look-alikes answering different questions stay, and the record says on which axis | A |\n| YIN collapse | fewer parts; every survivor earns its place by a named reader or question | B phases 1–2, 4–5 |\n| Aftermath / Evergreen | a dated reading carries its date; a live claim has a machine twin | B phase 3 (the mark) |\n| L-Prime | prose names what a thing DOES; remaining copulas carry a confidence marker | B phase 6, scoped in D |\n\nOrder matters: collapse before the record pass (so the record describes the collapsed tree once), the mark before any figure is \"corrected\" (so a corrected figure cannot drift again), L-Prime last (so prose is touched once, after the moves).\n\n## 0.1 Where the poles' numbers differ, and which difference matters\n\n| Figure | YIN | YANG | Why | Matters? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| fixtures whose vocabulary a snapshot carries | 50 of 87 | 60 of 87 | extraction width | No — both reject vocabulary subsumption as the criterion (C1); the ruling rests on YANG's 56-pin-a-law reading. |\n| OWED rows ablation / darkness | 330/359, 93/111 | 319, 92 | line grep vs reason-split | No — the distinct-cause counts (22 and 5, YANG, every row read) drive C4 and are robust to method. Use YANG's rows for the ~400-line estimate. |\n| container stacks identical | header 44/65 | YANG re-run 65/65 | dated header integer vs fresh reading | Only as an instance of the dated-reading defect (C5); the load-bearing claim holds either way. |\n| `READER … OWED` rows | 76, all darkness | 76: 65 darkness, 7 ablation, 4 expected-divergence | YANG finer | Yes — all three files are read by stripping readers, so NO live fault today; the latent fault is swallow-ledger (5 READER rows, 0 OWED, read by light-cone without stripping). Step 1 targets that file. |\n| fixture population | 76+11(+7 attic), \"87–89\" | 96 (76+11+6 attic+2 known-gaps+1 samples) | population definition; attic 7 vs 6 unverified | Yes for scope: the fixture ruling covers the 87 shared; attic/known-gaps/samples are protected separately (E). |\n| still.js:35-38 class count | header 8; YIN measured 13 (summing to 186 = still's 186) | — | stale comment | Yes — it caused YIN to rank a destructive collapse first in wave 1. Fix under the mark. |\n| `source ./grammars.sh` inlined | twice | once (the other file reads it as a file) | YANG read the act | Yes — follow YANG; one to fix. |\n| instruments | 65 non-test tools | 35 instruments / 49 gates | different populations | Only for the \"Seventeen instruments\" fix: say which population, or derive. |\n| theme-model readers | 12 requirers | 12 non-test readers, 8 gates, 18 requirers | YANG finer | Only for wording \"Four gates\". |\n\n## A. The intent map\n\nSix axes from the poles: population, scope, well-formedness, reader, grain, authority.\n\n**Q1. Does the grammar tokenize a text as pinned?** 40 snapshots (737 scopes, YIN) — records presence only, no syntax for absence (YANG). 87 fixtures — 1305 lines / 415 scopes (YIN); 36 carry negatives, 138 total (YANG). DIFFERENT GRAIN from snapshots on absence and on construct presence (six of seven `macro-dynamic-params` forms in zero snapshots, YANG). Only 4 behaviour-only fixtures (YANG): `blockquote`, `macro-string-params`, `mvv-display`, `pragma-params-mvv`, 127 lines. `snap-tid`+`snap-meta` — ONE SHAPE (both concede). `run_snapshots.sh`, `echo-test`, `list-test` — no reader. The four `tests-*` aliases — narrowings (see F.1). Attic (6/7), known-gaps (2), samples (1) — deliberately outside every glob (YANG), protected.\n\n**Q2. Where does the grammar disagree with the TW5 engine, and is each disagreement ruled?** `overreach` 31 exclusives · `-corpus-files` 57 · `-corpus-memetic` 2 · `-host` 2 · `-cut` 0; union 101 of 111; 10 unused = exactly the 10 `READER 5.5.0-prerelease` rulings keyed out by reader-scope.js (all YANG). `expected-divergence`, `divergence-staleness` (run set FROM package.json — YIN A4 :48-51), `reader-scope.js`, `degraded-ground.test.js`. DIFFERENT GRAIN on population; overreach-check.js:306 takes one pattern only, so the glob fusion is STRUCK by YIN itself. overreach-cut: C3.\n\n**Q3. Does the engine compile it, and behave as the model predicts?** `engine-witness` vs `engine-behaviour` (compile vs behaviour; the one engine-ledger ruling is BEHAVIOUR-prefixed, YANG) — keep. `theme-model` vs `theme-collision` (model vs the only reader of what vscode-textmate paints) — keep.\n\n**Q4. How much corpus is read fully; what remains unasked?** `still` (sampled; seeds 1/2/9/13 green, 5 red on one tree) vs `still --reach` (whole; floor 0.9947; 23 of 4,403 carriers unnamed, so a draw of 25 misses all 23 seven times in eight — YANG). Keep both. `swallow-witness` — same 186 instances as still (YIN A5) but alone yields `unasked-regions-ceiling` (97 regions, 83 open under some cut, 14 unasked) and an 18-region probe-escape reading. DIFFERENT QUESTION; fusion struck by YIN, defended by YANG — closed. `carrier-reach-floor`, `coverage-floor`, `ruling-breadth-ceiling`, `still-breadth.js` (child process in sandboxes). YANG names \"six coverage authorities\" without listing them; I do not map the sixth. `carrier-ledger` (7 rows) vs `swallow-ledger`: identical row grammar; header refuses fusion; `still --over ./corpus --reach` reads 52/52, 100.0%, floor 99.5%, never consulting the corpus ledger (YIN A3) — consistent, not proven (F.4).\n\n**Q5. Containment.** Five grains (YANG): bleed-canary / composition-check / swallow-witness / memetic-containment / corpus-check; plus canary-tid (2) and canary-memetic (4) — unmeasured against memetic-containment. bleed-canary vs corpus-check: three sentinel STRINGS, two baseline derivations (oracle `readAt().kind==='built'` vs a written control file). ONE SHAPE for strings; DIFFERENT GRAIN for baselines. Both agree: share strings only.\n\n**Q6. Can anything reach a scope?** scope-can-appear / grammar-reachability / corpus-check coverage — three causes (YANG). Keep; uncontested.\n\n**Q7. Legibility under themes.** dark-construct (absent rule) / contrast-witness (within CIE76 ΔE of default) / theme-parity (below the median of six comparators) — three MECHANISMS (YANG); 22 vs 26 findings, union 47, intersection 1 (YIN A1). Keep three; one home for the anecdote. colour-witness, colour-pair (ledger AND floor), legibility-floor; prose-reading-ledger (1 row) vs PlainConstructs.tid (20 keys): intersection 0, split by fault right, by storage arbitrary (YIN A2). theme-paint / family-atlas / page-palette / reading-recipe — HELD (F.11). uri-span-measure/compare — PROTECTED. Theme population: node_modules/tm-themes hardcoded in five instruments; 65; `BAR = 16` literal vs \"a quarter of 65\" prose (YIN R4).\n\n**Q8. Which rulings are owed, which hold, what retires?** Six `/^OWED/` readings: ablation-witness:361, darkness-witness:219, swallow-witness:107-108 strip `READER <v>`; light-cone:81, bracket-witness:155, delimiter-inheritance.test:96,106 do not (YANG A3). ONE SHAPE: `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()`. 12 ledger-shaped files, 10 named `-ledger`; 7 ratchets, 4 floor/3 ceiling; `attribute-kind-ceiling` may FALL (YIN V1). Lifecycle: stale/explains nothing/retires/unruled/idle — winner `idle` at divergence-staleness:137. `MISS` homonym (YIN V3). Ablation 359 rows / darkness 111 — 22 and 5 causes (YANG): C4.\n\n**Q9. Does the harness guard itself?** every-gate-collides — MEASURED FALSE GREEN (name over raw text, clause over stripped code; YANG; YIN B1 lines 67/77). Four CI gates outside it; package-contents.js has no test and no collider. No invariant enters the pairing — exemption by construction, recorded nowhere (YIN B4 21/39 with collider; YANG 25/39 without marker — different markers, neither matters once written down). one-implementation's `*.test.js` exclusion: C2. every-test-runs sees no fixture (YANG). gate-report --check NOT read-only: `ceiling` and `builtins` write tracked files (YANG; YIN B2 names the law and two correct precedents). SKIP regex vs reasons list — two keyed enumerations (YIN R8), HELD (F.5). CI: `compose` is the only true duplicate (same ubuntu/node22 as gates, YIN B3); grammar job is a 4-way matrix; test.yml:88-95 is what makes four gates blocking (YANG) — PROTECTED; :60-69 dirty-tree guard runs in `grammar`, not `gates`.\n\n**Q10. Does the record match the tree?** Migration headline in four places, three regexes; MIGRATION:36 and SCOPE-NAMES:20 say 111 for certified 110; LEDGER:1294 says 585/122/247 vs 556/110/245 (YIN; YANG concedes, adds \"one file contradicts itself 31 lines apart\"). \"65 themes\" in 8 files, welded nowhere (YIN R3); 106 N/65 figures with two welds reading UNRELEASED only (YANG); 6 `# checks:` twins in the whole repo, none in the LEDGER (YIN). README gate list: 25 names, 3 duplicate bullets, 37 of 49 unnamed, weld checks existence only (YIN R6). Four wrong counts (all confirmed by YANG): \"Thirteen\" (20), \"Seventeen instruments\" (49/35/65), \"Four gates\" (8 gates / 12 non-test readers / 18 requirers), \"Twenty-two\" (26 non-test / 35). Three colour header integers reproduce in rank/ratio, not integer (YANG A2). ONE SHAPE: a figure is dated or derived — the mark.\n\n**Q11. What ships?** `.vscodeignore`, `package-contents.js` (manifest→package only). `vsce ls`: 34 files; syntaxes/attic 14,013+936 bytes; docs/prior-art seven documents 280,996 bytes; nine .mem + attic 349,604 bytes (YIN A6, listing only). `.vscodeignore:16` references run_snapshots.sh (YANG).\n\n**Q12. Does the grammar stall?** backtrack-witness — wall-clock: 1.4 ms alone vs past 8 ms under the suite; 0 vs 6 stalls at rest (YANG). Keep; re-measure after every phase that changes what runs beside it.\n\n## B. The ordered plan\n\n### Phase 0 — make the verifier honest\n**0.1** every-gate-collides strips comments before the NAME match. Lost: nothing; at least one green gate will red (YIN B1) — that red is the finding. Evidence: YANG fault 1; corpus-ledgers.test.js:43 is the worked example. Why before step 1: every later move/delete of a test file is certified by this invariant, and step 1 must carry delimiter-inheritance.test.js:104-107's collider across (YIN B3).\n**0.2** the manifest names only --check arms (`ceiling` → textmate-ceiling.js --check; `builtins` → builtins-sync.js --check). Evidence: YANG fault 2; YIN B2's law and precedents (edition:build/check, signals/signals:check). The hand runs `gate-report --check` after every phase; today that dirties the tree twice.\n**0.3** write the exemption down: invariants enter no collider pairing by construction; the four CI gates outside the invariant listed by name. Evidence: YANG 4–5, YIN B4.\n\n### Phase 1 — the one latent fault that disarms a gate\n**1.1** one `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()`; six sites call it. Lost: nothing today (all 76 rows sit in stripping readers, YANG 65/7/4). First: 0.1. Evidence: YANG A3 — light-cone and swallow-witness read the SAME file with incompatible predicates; swallow-ledger holds five READER rows, zero OWED; add OWED to one and light-cone's one-sided gate reads it RULED and goes silent. Collider: a `READER 5.4.1 OWED` row in a sandboxed swallow-ledger must red light-cone after and be shown green-by-silence before.\n**Do I agree with \"first\"?** On substance yes: it precedes every collapse, since every ledger rename (phase 4) and the backlog re-key (C4) passes through this reader, and a re-key through six divergent predicates is six faults. On the literal position no: phase 0 is what makes 1.1's verification trustworthy and costs three lines. If the hand can take one step only, take 1.1.\n\n### Phase 2 — pure removals\n**2.1** delete `run_snapshots.sh` + `echo-test` + `list-test` AND `.vscodeignore:16` together (YANG's coupling: the package gate never reports a stale ignore entry).\n**2.2** strike the four narrowing aliases (82 → 75, YIN). First: F.1.\n**2.3** strike CI `compose`. Must NOT touch test.yml:88-95 or the matrix.\n**2.4** fuse snap-tid + snap-meta. Lost: a harvest summary line — YANG: habit, no file states 49. First: 0.1 and F.3.\n**2.5** `scopesOn` ×2 → tokenizer.js's helper; the one inlined `source ./grammars.sh` → the shared act; rename the third same-named different function (YANG A4). No ward change needed.\n**2.6** share the three sentinel STRINGS; keep both baseline derivations.\n\n### Phase 3 — the mark, then every figure under it\n**3.1** ONE syntax for a figure: `<figure> (read <date>, over <population>)` or a machine twin — reuse the `# checks:` form already in 6 places, never a second. ONE gate: a figure in a welded file carrying neither fails; keyed on the mark, NOT on UNRELEASED (both existing welds go blind when 3.1.0 opens — YANG). Position: after phases 1–2 so derived figures describe the collapsed tree; before 3.2–3.8 so each fix is an instance of the mark. YANG wanted it second; the only difference is letting the pure removals go first because they change counts the mark would otherwise date twice.\n**3.2** one home for the migration headline; MIGRATION:36 and SCOPE-NAMES:20 111→110; LEDGER:1294's 585/122/247 marked as the dated sequence it narrates, not corrected; three regexes → one weld on the mark. Caution F.2 (110 vs 111) before editing.\n**3.3** weld the theme count (\"65 as this repository bundles them\"); derive BAR from it.\n**3.4** fix the four counts WITHOUT deleting paragraphs — each derived or dated, population named.\n**3.5** still.js:35-38 8 → 13, dated.\n**3.6** the three colour header integers get date and population; do NOT overwrite with YANG's re-run (C5). Anecdote to ONE home; each header keeps one line naming its MECHANISM.\n**3.7** generate the README gate list's completeness CHECK; keep curated prose; --check arm only in the manifest.\n**3.8** move gate-report.js:18-25 to LEDGER:1809-1812 (already holds it); carry 38-46's routing LAW into the LEDGER while LEAVING the comment in place (no test holds it).\n\n### Phase 4 — vocabulary (after phase 1; every rename passes through owedOf/readerOf and ledger-shape)\n**4.1** `-ledger`/`-ratchet` names, direction in the first comment line (confirm `attribute-kind-ceiling` first, F.6); collider obligations move with names. **4.2** `MISS` → `dark`/`unmarked`. **4.3** `idle`/`unruled`/`retired`. **4.4** one spelling of overreach (YIN V2), weld-grep first.\n\n### Phase 5 — conditionals\n**5.1** attic (and docs/prior-art) out of the .vsix: build AND EXTRACT first; land with package-contents' first collider; add package→needed. Attic stays in the tree. **5.2** retire overreach-cut: C3. **5.3** backlog collapse: C4. **5.4** fuse the four behaviour-only fixtures once each has a snapshot sample; fix `blockquote`'s wrong header regardless. **5.5** one home for judgements (corpus text vs JSON tiddlers): record the axis per surface; move no data until read. **5.6** four colour CLI surfaces — HELD. **5.7** canary-memetic vs memetic-containment — HELD.\n\n### Phase 6 — L-Prime / Evergreen, once (D).\n\n## C. Adjudications\n\n**C1 Fixtures (50 vs 60; subsumption).** Vocabulary subsumption is NOT safe; the 50/60 gap is irrelevant. Follow YANG: 36 of 87 carry 138 negatives and snapshots have no absence syntax (29 of the 60 lost outright); construct presence ≠ vocabulary presence (six of seven macro-dynamic-params forms in zero snapshots, one under live OWED). YIN itself handed the law question over. 4 fusible, 83 stay. Would change it: an absence-recording snapshot format AND a scope-at-position measurement — both, not either.\n\n**C2 The ward's `.test.js` exclusion.** Keep it; extend the existing five-entry named-exemption map to the fingerprint scan (YANG A4). The reason two lines above the exclusion is decisive: a test must hold its gate's collider, and the no-second-implementation rule on tests would forbid the collision the house requires. Lifting widens obligations (YIN B1 concedes). The two duplications are fixed in 2.5 without the ward. Would change it: the map cannot express \"a test may carry its collided instrument's body\" — then a new map entry kind, still no blanket lift.\n\n**C3 overreach-cut.** YANG's condition, YANG's order: fix degraded-ground.test.js's host resolution so it RUNS in CI (today it skips unless a TW checkout is a sibling; a skip reads as a pass), confirm a run not a skip, then drop the script — and re-confirm 0 exclusives at that moment (it is a property of the current ruling file, not of the arm; divergence-staleness derives from package.json). Would change it: a non-zero exclusive after the fix, or no way to give CI a host.\n\n**C4 Backlogs and the one-cause ratchet.** YANG's concession, YANG's condition, non-negotiable: `cause` identifier distinct from `key`; breadth ratchet counts causes; ratchet seated at 1 refuses a ruling absorbing more than one cause, header stating why (predecessor re-seated 55.8→56.6→57.2→60.0% in one session, every reason true). 22 and 5 causes at character-position grain forced by the key grammar (darkness's 89-row cause is restated in its own header). 330/93 vs 319/92 is method; untouched. Order: after phase 1 and 4.1. Would change it: a row-grain reader nobody named.\n\n**C5 Colour header integers.** Dated readings in the present tense — \"one defect, not two\" (YANG). Rank/direction/ratio reproduce (variable first both times; 9.7% vs 10.1%); integers and populations moved (59 vs 54 themes; 15,116 vs 11,756). Do not rewrite 44→65; date the 44 with its population, or replace with a derivation producing a machine twin. Three gates stay (fusion loses 46 of 47 findings, YIN). Would change it: a shipped derivation script — then no integer in the header at all.\n\n**Closed by the poles, do not reopen:** swallow ⊂ still; dark-construct ∪ contrast-witness; the overreach glob fusion; prose-reading-ledger ∪ PlainConstructs; the three flag-pairs as \"one tool two gates\" (flags switch POPULATION, YANG; YIN accepts).\n\n## D. Evergreen / L-Prime, as work (densities are YIN's; YANG did not verify)\n\n**Touches, by yield:** (1) harness comment archaeology — gate-report.js:18-25 (moved in 3.8); coverage-floor's header (13 of 24 lines narrate two re-seats → one dated line, history to the LEDGER); ruling-breadth-ceiling and must-fail headers. (2) LEDGER: 127 copulas at 0.07/line, explanatory tails (\"which is\", \"is the\", \"is what\") — turn the tails; copulas stating a ruling stay with a confidence marker; the 106 figures go through the mark, not prose. (3) README/MIGRATION/CHANGELOG at 0.04–0.06 — CHANGELOG's past entries are dated by construction, touch only UNRELEASED; MIGRATION sentences a weld reads change only WITH the weld. (4) the four count paragraphs — number fixed under the mark, sentence turned to say what the count GUARDS.\n\n**Must not touch:** docs/scope-naming-prior-art.mem — 84 of 87 copulas inside a VERBATIM handback; only the 3 outside are in scope. contributing.md — zero copulas. The 19 load-bearing sites (E): rephrase in place, never move/shorten/delete unless the law is first carried into a test or LEDGER row. Any weld-read sentence. Quoted error strings, operator-spoken rulings, fixture header lines stating a law (4, YANG).\n\n**Three questions per sentence:** (1) inside a fence/quotation/verbatim block? leave it. (2) does an instrument read it? change only with that reader, red first. (3) does it state a law nothing else holds? keep content word-for-word, turn only the copula, never move it alone. Three no's → turn freely: name what it does, date any number, derive any count.\n\n## E. Refused from any tidy-up (thing · why it looks removable · read first)\n- LEDGER:856-861 within-construct witness DEFERRED BY RULING · 851-855 fragment unarticulated on purpose · 780-790 underline one stroke · 836-850 two REFUSED palette moves.\n- uri-span-measure / uri-span-compare