tion. Before 4.1.\n7. The 63 punctuation.separator sites — fifth naming law or accretion. Out of scope until read.\n8. backtrack-witness under the collapsed suite — re-measure after phases 2 and 5.\n9. What reads the 6 `# checks:` twins — the mark must reuse it, not add a second reader.\n10. A .vsix extracted, not listed — settles 5.1.\n11. The four CLI colour surfaces and canary-memetic — held until read.\n12. Copula densities — YIN's only; a second count before phase 6 is cheap.\n\n## G. Short form\n0. Collider strips comments before the name match · manifest names only --check arms · write the invariants' exemption down.\n1. `owedOf()` beside `readerOf()`, six sites, collider carried, red-first on a sandboxed swallow-ledger.\n2. Three dead scripts + `.vscodeignore:16` · four aliases (after F.1) · CI compose · snap-tid/snap-meta · two duplications + one misnamed function · three sentinel strings.\n3. The dated-or-derived mark with one gate keyed on it · then headline/110 (after F.2), theme count + BAR, four counts, 8→13, colour integers dated, README check generated, gate-report archaeology moved.\n4. `-ledger`/`-ratchet` with direction · MISS → dark/unmarked · idle/unruled/retired · one spelling of overreach.\n5. Conditionals behind their conditions: attic out of the .vsix with package-contents' first collider · overreach-cut after degraded-ground runs in CI · backlogs after the cause field and one-cause ratchet · four fixtures after their samples exist.\n6. L-Prime/Evergreen once, with D's three questions, never inside the verbatim handback."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfoCpHngcP9Erb27ZFny3","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"530789f5-d57c-46d3-a7ae-55ece1c9e397","timestamp":"2026-10-07T16:39:21.978Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/VSCode-TW5-Syntax","sessionId":"7bdba225-51